00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:35.310
- When do you start getting a
thought that, like, what is,

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:36.300
what the fuck is this thing?

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.550
- So, that happened when
we visually saw one.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.846
There were two aircraft
from my squadron, VFA 11,

00:10:42.846 --> 00:10:46.182
and they flew, took
off as a flight of two.

00:10:46.182 --> 00:10:48.480
That means they're essentially
flying in a formation

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.980
like this.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:50.837
And as they hit the area,

00:10:50.837 --> 00:10:53.220
one of these objects went
right between the aircraft.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:56.580
- We have a very strict
system for controlling

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:59.070
who is flying in our airspace to make sure

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.450
that things don't run into each other

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:02.250
because random stuff flying around

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:05.040
could risk the lives of the pilots

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.140
and these $67 million weapons.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.600
So, when something like this
happens, it's a huge deal.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.520
They immediately abort
whatever they're doing,

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.410
and they return to their ship to, like,

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.480
discuss what the hell just happened.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.687
- And you know, he was
just sitting there saying,

00:11:16.687 --> 00:11:19.200
"Hey, you know, I almost hit
one of those damn things,"

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:20.910
and we all knew what he was referring to,

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.740
even though we didn't
necessarily have a name for it

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.390
just because we were seeing these so much.

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:25.590
And he described it, you know.

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:28.980
He described it just as a
black or dark gray cube.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:33.210
And that cube was inside of a
clear or translucent sphere,

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:36.450
and essentially the the apex
with the corners of that cube,

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:37.321
best he could tell,

00:11:37.321 --> 00:11:40.080
were touching that inside of that sphere.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:41.340
- Wait, hold on. Did you catch that?

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:44.850
Not the weird cube inside of a
translucent sphere, whatever.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:45.683
We'll get to that later.

00:11:45.683 --> 00:11:46.890
To me, what's actually more compelling

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:48.630
about what this guy just said is.

00:11:48.630 --> 00:11:50.100
- Because we were seeing these so much.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.930
- He is saying that these pilots

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:52.807
have been seeing these things.

00:11:52.807 --> 00:11:55.203
- You know, essentially, all the time.

00:11:55.203 --> 00:11:57.630
- Wow. Yeah.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:58.463
Like yeah, I get it.

00:11:58.463 --> 00:12:01.170
The translucent cube thing
is, like, more tantalizing,

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:03.270
but, like, the fact
that these pilots report

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:07.920
seeing these UAPs, these UFOs,
all the time, day after day,

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:11.220
week after week, that, to me,
is more compelling evidence

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:12.510
that we need to evaluate here.

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:15.300
And, like the 2004 Tic Tac
case that we talked about

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:16.133
at the beginning.

00:12:16.133 --> 00:12:17.850
- This was happening because
we upgraded our radar,

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:18.683
the best we could tell.

00:12:18.683 --> 00:12:21.270
- These Navy personnel
at first don't believe

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:22.103
what they're seeing.

00:12:22.103 --> 00:12:24.000
They think that their
instruments are probably broken.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.121
- And then people started to
try to fly by it and see it.

00:12:26.121 --> 00:12:27.428
And at this point, you know,

00:12:27.428 --> 00:12:30.270
I would say maybe 80
to 90% of our squadron

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.040
had probably seen one of these
on the radar at this point.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:33.090
Everyone was aware of it.

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:34.890
- So, according to some of these accounts,

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:38.460
you've got a bunch of Navy
pilots seeing weird stuff

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:40.620
all the time, both on radar

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:42.360
but also with their infrared cameras.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:45.570
But are you gonna be the guy
who goes to your superior

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:49.110
in the Navy and say, like,
hey, I saw another UFO today.

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:51.030
You don't wanna be like the UFO crazy.

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:52.770
You're gonna get kicked
out of the freaking, like,

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:56.820
most superior pilot corps
in the world because, like,

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:58.020
you're seeing UFOs.

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.257
These pilots have talked about
how there's a real stigma

00:13:00.257 --> 00:13:02.010
with reporting this stuff,

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:03.630
so a lot of 'em just sort of keep quiet.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:06.240
But it was when that near
crash happened that now

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:09.570
these pilots are literally
required to file safety reports

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:10.403
of what happened.

00:13:10.403 --> 00:13:12.715
And this is where the Pentagon
and lawmakers who fund them

00:13:12.715 --> 00:13:15.870
were forced to take these
UFOs more seriously.

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:19.650
- We know that our service
members have encountered

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.930
unidentified aerial phenomenon,

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:24.810
and because UAPs pose
potential flight safety

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:25.892
and general security risk,

00:13:25.892 --> 00:13:28.590
we are committed to a focused effort

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:29.970
to determine their origins.

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:32.550
- This is where I start
to get pretty excited

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:33.840
about the potential here because, look,

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:38.670
this is like a real high up
person in our intel community

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:40.950
in the military who's talking about

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:43.170
getting more data on this, on studying it.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:44.670
Keep going. Mr. Moultrie.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:47.220
- Our effort will include
the thorough examination

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.470
of adversarial platforms

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.810
and potential breakthrough technologies,

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.020
US government or commercial platforms,

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:59.020
allied or partner systems
and other natural phenomenon.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.380
- Scientists, military leaders,

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:04.500
even some politicians
are joining the crowd

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:08.460
of true believers with the
US Navy task force called in.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:10.800
- So, by 2020 this is now,
like, becoming a thing,

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.288
and this is probably why
you've heard about it recently.

00:14:12.288 --> 00:14:14.577
This task force was
formed, and it represents

00:14:14.577 --> 00:14:17.529
the first time since 1969
that the US government

00:14:17.529 --> 00:14:21.300
has officially or at least
publicly acknowledged

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:23.850
the significance of studying UFOs.

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:24.720
- There is something there,

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:26.370
measurable by multiple instruments,

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:28.410
and yet, it seems to move in directions

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:31.410
that are inconsistent with
what we know of physics

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:33.060
or science more broadly.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.418
And that, to me, poses
questions of tremendous interest

00:14:36.418 --> 00:14:41.418
and, as well as potential
national security significance.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:44.220
- Okay, wait, pause, just, yep.

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:46.320
Inconsistent with the
laws of physics. Yep.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:47.970
Very tantalizing. Let's just pause.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:50.688
We're talking about UFOs
here, and I feel obligated

00:14:50.688 --> 00:14:52.440
to just check in

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.270
and make sure we're all
on the same page, okay?

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:57.870
First, we know it is a
fact that the US government

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:00.930
has observed stuff in the
air that they can't explain.

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:03.300
The evidence that I've
presented here is solid,

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.820
solid sources, solid reporting.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:08.580
If I had evidence like
this for any other story

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:10.230
that I'm doing, I'd be like,
this is solid evidence.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:11.760
Let's put it in the story. Okay?

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.552
We know that it's true.

00:15:13.552 --> 00:15:16.020
(suspenseful music)

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:17.460
Oh, and it's not just the few events

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:18.293
that I've mentioned here.

00:15:18.293 --> 00:15:21.810
According to this report, there's been 144

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:24.510
of these instances either
from the US military

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:25.620
or government personnel,

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:29.400
and 80 of these reports have been gathered

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.290
from quote, "multiple sensors,"

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:32.970
meaning from multiple perspectives,

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.590
multiple perspectives or tools,

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:37.170
which is like a thousand
times better than, like,

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:40.260
one pilot just saw something
and is remembering it.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:42.360
Even if said pilot is someone like

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:44.130
Lieutenant Commander Alex Dietrich,

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.140
who, when you read this profile
from "The Washington Post"

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:49.687
on her, seems to be a pragmatic,
highly credible Navy pilot

00:15:49.687 --> 00:15:51.600
from one of the most
specialized flight programs

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:52.433
in the world.

00:15:52.433 --> 00:15:55.950
- I don't identify as a UFO person.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:57.720
- Like, these pilots don't have incentives

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:58.740
to make this stuff up.

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:01.110
And yet, the fact remains
that their instruments

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:03.360
for measuring and observing the world

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:06.030
is the human eyes, brain
and long-term memory,

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:07.650
which is a pretty faulty and inaccurate

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:08.610
data collection tool.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:11.430
So, when I see something
like 80 of these sightings

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:14.370
being collected from multiple sensors,

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:15.510
it makes all the difference for me.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:16.680
Okay, so that's number one.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:17.790
The US government has seen this.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.980
They don't know what it is,
and it's been collected well.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:22.170
Number two, the other thing we know

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:23.940
is that they've taken it seriously.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:24.930
This is a concern for them.

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:27.570
The US Department of
Defense is funding an effort

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:30.960
to investigate, study and
analyze what is happening here,

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:32.700
which, again, is awesome.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:35.910
Funding research is the only
way that we know anything

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:36.743
about the world.

00:16:36.743 --> 00:16:38.880
It's so much better than
hearing a few people riff

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:39.750
on what they saw.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:41.748
Science and research is our best antidote

00:16:41.748 --> 00:16:44.640
to the faulty, story driven human brain.

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:47.100
And indeed, the task force has come to

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:49.740
some pretty useful conclusions.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:51.193
- Since the release of
that preliminary report,

00:16:51.193 --> 00:16:54.720
UAP task force database
has now grown to contain

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.910
approximately 400 reports.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.050
- They went back and they looked at

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.160
every one of these reports,

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.450
analyzed all the data they could.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.520
And when you do that, you
start to see these incidents

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:03.930
come into perspective.

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:06.600
Remember this video of the
fast moving round thing

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.130
that the pilot was freaking out about?

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:10.140
Turns out that the Pentagon analyzed this,

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:12.000
knowing everything they know
about where the jets were

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.370
and what tools were being
used to record this moment.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:16.860
And they calculated that
this was actually just, like,

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.690
an optical illusion.

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:20.850
Like, this object actually
isn't moving that fast,

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:22.110
only like 30 miles an hour.

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:24.333
Or remember this video of
the triangles in the sky

00:17:24.333 --> 00:17:26.460
filmed off of that destroyer?

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:29.130
It turns out that this was
more just quirky optics.

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:31.410
- [Scott] We're now reasonably confident

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:32.760
that these triangles correlate

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:35.100
to unmanned aerial systems in the area.

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:38.640
The triangular appearance
is a result of light

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:40.234
passing through the night vision goggles

00:17:40.234 --> 00:17:42.630
and then being recorded by an SLR camera.

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:45.780
- These objects are
probably foreign drones

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:48.150
trying to spy on US military maneuvers,

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:50.160
yet they might not be triangle in shape,

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:52.650
but, like, that's still
really useful information.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:54.840
We should know if there
are foreign adversaries

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.000
floating over our Navy destroyers.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.490
Or this video of a UFO shaped object

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:00.913
being chased by an F-18.

00:18:00.913 --> 00:18:02.670
- [Pilot] There's a whole
fleet of them. Look on the ASA.

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:04.050
- What makes this video so weird is

00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:06.030
how the object is behaving,

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:09.483
unexpected ways, kind
of turning and rotating.

00:18:11.022 --> 00:18:12.829
- [Pilot 2] Look at that thing.

00:18:12.829 --> 00:18:14.640
- [Pilot] It's rotating.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.800
- Well, once again with
a little bit of analysis,

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.680
this weird movement is
actually just another quirk

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:22.320
of the image sensors that
they use in the military

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:24.262
on these specialized
cameras that make objects

00:18:24.262 --> 00:18:26.569
look like they're moving in strange ways,

00:18:26.569 --> 00:18:28.590
when, really, if you just
saw it with your eye,

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:29.730
it wouldn't be that weird.

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:30.990
There's this guy, Mick West,

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:33.180
who's probably the most
passionate debunker of, like,

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:34.950
anything weird going on here.

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:36.674
He does a really compelling deep dive on

00:18:36.674 --> 00:18:38.520
an explanation for this,

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:40.650
why this object looks like
it's moving so strangely.

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:41.820
I mean if you want to go into it,

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:45.780
it's like another optical
mixed with camera sensors

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:47.580
mixed with gimbal equipment

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:49.538
and rotating compensation mechanisms.

00:18:49.538 --> 00:18:51.330
Yeah, you get the point,

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:53.160
but we still don't know
what this object is,

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:54.828
but at least we have more clarity

00:18:54.828 --> 00:18:58.260
on why it looks weird to us with our eyes

00:18:58.260 --> 00:18:59.880
when we're watching on
a video on the internet.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:02.490
The Pentagon recently came out
and told "The New York Times"

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:04.590
that most of this stuff is actually

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:07.410
just foreign spies flying around,

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:11.220
spying on US military
activities or weather balloons

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:12.390
or other airborne tracks,

00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:15.150
and further specifying
that a lot of this stuff

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:17.160
that looks weird to us looks weird

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:20.580
because it was recorded
on gear that is classified

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:22.440
and is built for a specific purpose

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:24.660
that we don't have
access to understanding,

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:26.610
leading to some strange looking imagery.

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:28.383
Really convenient, Pentagon.

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:31.740
And yet, another fact
in all of this is that

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:34.530
many of these videos have
not been officially declared

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:38.610
a foreign drone and, in
fact, remain unexplained.

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:40.290
And that's after analysis.

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:44.190
One of those unexplained
sightings was this one from 2004,

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:47.355
the one we started this video
on, the Tic Tac incident.

00:19:47.355 --> 00:19:50.130
(suspenseful music)

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:54.150
The report often cites lack
of good data and, indeed,

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:55.950
what we have here is not the best,

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:58.110
but we still have four sets of eyeballs.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:00.750
We have an official Navy
report gathering facts

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:01.583
from that day,

00:20:01.583 --> 00:20:05.100
technicians seeing this thing
descend from 60,000 feet

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.750
down to 50 feet in a matter of seconds,

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:10.380
hovering stationary on the
radar for a short amount of time

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:13.680
and then departing at high
velocities, high turn rates.

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:16.710
This video, which is kind
of uninspiring and grainy

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:19.920
and not very long, but
still shows us something,

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.980
with its infrared not
capturing any heat signature,

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:26.070
any means of propulsion
as this thing flies around

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:28.413
at mind boggling speeds.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.970
Since these pilots went
public with their account,

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:35.940
a handful more of Navy
witnesses have come forward

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.220
telling their stories
of what they have seen.

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:40.170
And again, I take this all
with a giant grain of salt,

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.480
especially when you see
some of these accounts

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:45.066
putting fuel on the fire
in the form of crazy claims

00:20:45.066 --> 00:20:47.430
that, I'm intentionally not
gonna go into into them here

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:50.280
because I consider them
deeply outside of the realm

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:51.450
of useful evidence.

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:52.380
But yeah, if you're interested,

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:53.790
you can easily go down the rabbit hole.

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.620
This stuff is like
clickbait for every human.

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:56.700
If you do go down the rabbit hole

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:59.130
on some of these other
testimonies or witnesses,

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:00.360
just be careful.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.370
This is powerful, intoxicating stuff.

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:04.170
We all secretly want to believe

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:06.090
that this isn't just,
like, China spying on us.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:06.923
That's boring.

00:21:06.923 --> 00:21:08.880
Our brains are really good
at filling in the gaps

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:10.553
to construct a faulty narrative.

00:21:10.553 --> 00:21:11.490
Be careful.

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:14.700
But yeah, that aside, there's
still no satisfying theories

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:17.760
that I could find that
explain the 2004 Tic Tac case.

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:19.885
Could be Russia or Chinese secret drones

00:21:19.885 --> 00:21:22.440
or even experimental aircraft

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:24.390
that we ourselves have been developing.

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:26.670
I mean, it's no secret
that powerful countries

00:21:26.670 --> 00:21:29.220
spend a lot of time and
resources trying to get

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.780
a leg up militarily, trying to find

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:32.080
the next big technological thing.

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:35.940
Like, you can actually find
patents from the US military

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:39.360
that claim to revolutionize
propulsion tech

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:43.050
using, like, anti-gravity
spacecraft, like,

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:46.826
really out there, wild,
weird, theoretical tech

00:21:46.826 --> 00:21:48.990
that may or may not exist.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:50.880
Again, another rabbit hole
I'm not gonna go down.

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:53.910
The 2004 Tic Tac case remains a mystery,

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:55.920
and I have a feeling that it
will be a mystery forever.

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:58.380
We'll probably never
know what this thing is,

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:01.320
and that's because real answers only come

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:04.140
when you have real inquiry with real tools

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:07.470
to measure and analyze real
data from the real world.

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:09.119
People's eyes and brains and memories

00:22:09.119 --> 00:22:11.430
are about the worst
thing you can count on,

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:14.310
and yet, we can't ignore credible sources.

00:22:14.310 --> 00:22:15.720
- They were always out there, you know.

00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:16.553
- [Joe] Always.

00:22:16.553 --> 00:22:17.386
- They were out there when we took off.

00:22:17.386 --> 00:22:18.930
We'd see them and then we'd go to land.

00:22:18.930 --> 00:22:19.860
They would still be out there.

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:20.693
- Like every day?

00:22:20.693 --> 00:22:21.750
- Every day.

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:23.430
- But that's not proof of anything.

00:22:23.430 --> 00:22:25.710
To me, if they're always out there,

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:27.960
we should be able to come
up with a way to study them,

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:29.370
and the US government agrees.

00:22:29.370 --> 00:22:32.136
- This often limited
amount of high quality data

00:22:32.136 --> 00:22:35.580
and reporting hampers our
ability to draw firm conclusions

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:37.770
about the nature or intent of UAP.

00:22:37.770 --> 00:22:39.120
- Step one in all this is gonna be

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:41.370
to decouple the study of UFOs,

00:22:41.370 --> 00:22:42.565
which is something we should totally do,

00:22:42.565 --> 00:22:45.630
from the quick conclusion
that people jump to

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:47.370
that we are being visited by aliens

00:22:47.370 --> 00:22:48.450
from a different star system.

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:50.550
That is what created the
stigma in the first place.

00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:52.888
That is why people are embarrassed
to talk about this stuff.

00:22:52.888 --> 00:22:54.916
We need to decouple them. There are UFOs.

00:22:54.916 --> 00:22:56.970
We should study them and
see what they actually are.

00:22:56.970 --> 00:22:58.839
But am I saying that
these absolutely aren't

00:22:58.839 --> 00:23:02.310
alien spacecraft coming
from other planets?

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:04.320
No, I'm not saying that
at all. I don't know.

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:06.810
What I'm saying is that I
haven't seen anything close

00:23:06.810 --> 00:23:10.140
to the burden of evidence
required for me to believe

00:23:10.140 --> 00:23:11.880
that that's what these things are.

00:23:11.880 --> 00:23:14.610
What I have seen is evidence
of weird, unidentified things

00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:17.610
flying around, behaving in
ways that are potentially

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:20.190
beyond our mainstream
understanding of physics.

00:23:20.190 --> 00:23:21.030
I mean, potentially.

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:23.670
So yes, I'm totally open to
these things being aliens.

00:23:23.670 --> 00:23:25.350
I'm open to literally anything.

00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:28.020
My issue is that people see this,

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:30.600
and our brains automatically
do the easy thing,

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:31.980
which is to fill in the blanks.

00:23:31.980 --> 00:23:34.772
Suddenly, aliens are the
explanation. My brain does it, too.

00:23:34.772 --> 00:23:37.530
It scares me. It's not
the right approach here.

00:23:37.530 --> 00:23:39.030
I mean, I'm aware that it literally

00:23:39.030 --> 00:23:41.430
is almost a statistical impossibility

00:23:41.430 --> 00:23:44.340
that we're the only intelligent
life forms in this universe.

00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:45.510
Definitely not the the case.

00:23:45.510 --> 00:23:47.460
So yeah, maybe they found a way to travel

00:23:47.460 --> 00:23:49.260
to our little speck of dust planet,

00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:51.660
and they wanted to visit
and look at us or something.

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:52.493
I don't know.

00:23:52.493 --> 00:23:53.400
I'm totally open to it, but again,

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:54.990
I have zero reason to believe that

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:56.100
because there's no evidence

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:58.143
that points to that as the explanation.

00:23:59.087 --> 00:24:00.960
- [Announcer] Seven, six, five.

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:02.100
- But then there's the flip side,

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:04.020
the juicier part of this for me,

00:24:04.020 --> 00:24:05.970
which is, who's to say we aren't

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:08.550
the awe inspiring creatures ourselves?

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:09.390
A hundred years ago,

00:24:09.390 --> 00:24:12.330
most people were still
riding around on horses.

00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:15.010
They would've looked at our
modern world, all of this

00:24:17.250 --> 00:24:20.130
and thought that, certainly,
aliens had come to take over.

00:24:20.130 --> 00:24:22.740
Certainly, some crazy magician had come

00:24:22.740 --> 00:24:24.990
and reshaped the entire planet,

00:24:24.990 --> 00:24:26.700
and that's exactly what happened.

00:24:26.700 --> 00:24:29.190
Crazy scientific breakthroughs
happen all the time.

00:24:29.190 --> 00:24:31.590
I mean, just this year,
the Nobel Prize in physics

00:24:31.590 --> 00:24:34.050
went to a team of physicists
laying the foundation

00:24:34.050 --> 00:24:36.905
for quantum communication,
like real-time communication

00:24:36.905 --> 00:24:40.170
that essentially bypasses the
classical laws of physics.

00:24:40.170 --> 00:24:42.741
What I'm trying to say here
is we don't need to treat UFOs

00:24:42.741 --> 00:24:43.611
like religion.

00:24:43.611 --> 00:24:45.210
We don't need to believe.

00:24:45.210 --> 00:24:47.340
Instead of cobbling
together the scant evidence

00:24:47.340 --> 00:24:50.820
that we have to fit some
narrative that we want to believe,

00:24:50.820 --> 00:24:53.970
let's go out there and
gather data and analyze it

00:24:53.970 --> 00:24:56.100
and build a body of knowledge about this.

00:24:56.100 --> 00:24:58.530
Let's poke at these
phenomena and figure out

00:24:58.530 --> 00:25:00.420
what the hell is going on in our airspace,

00:25:00.420 --> 00:25:02.010
at the very least to keep us safe,

00:25:02.010 --> 00:25:04.410
but potentially so that we
can discover something new,

00:25:04.410 --> 00:25:07.679
something that we can
observe, measure, analyze

00:25:07.679 --> 00:25:09.033
and learn from.

00:25:11.640 --> 00:25:13.050
Wait, wait, wait, don't go yet.

00:25:13.050 --> 00:25:14.280
They released the report.

00:25:14.280 --> 00:25:16.140
The Pentagon released the report, like,

00:25:16.140 --> 00:25:17.700
right before we published this video.

00:25:17.700 --> 00:25:19.281
Like, we were waiting for
them to release the report,

00:25:19.281 --> 00:25:20.370
and then they didn't.

00:25:20.370 --> 00:25:22.620
So, we filmed the video and I cut my hair,

00:25:22.620 --> 00:25:26.250
